Remedies for Vomiting and how to stop vomiting.\nHome Remedies for Vomiting\n- Crush 2 cloves (laung) and boil in 100gm water for 15 minutes. After 15 minutes mix some misri or sugar in it, drink it and sleep sideways. Follow this procedure after every 4 hours will give you 100% relief in puking .\n- Clove is best home remedy for vomiting and nausea. Rub 2 cloves to make a thick paste and take it with 30gm hot water. Only chewing clove is also beneficial in puking, nausea, vertigo and bad breath of mouth.\n- If you have vomiting in pregnancy then rub 2 cloves with misri (candy sugar). Now mix this paste in half cup lukewarm water and drink.\n- If you feel vomiting during your journey in bus or train then chew 1 clove. It will give you instant relief.\n- If you have vomiting because of heat then take 12 gm coriander powder and soak in 250gm water for 1 hour. For taste mix 1 table spoon candy sugar in it. After one hour filter this water and give 1 table spoon of this water to children and 30gm to adults after every one hour. Its best home remedy for vomiting in summer season.\n- Take one big lemon and cut it in 2 parts. Now apply rock salt on one part and chew slowly. It will give you instant relief in puking and vertigo.\n- If you have hard vomiting then take one table spoon lime water, mix it in 125gm milk and drink 2 times in a day.\n- Mix one teaspoon of ginger juice with one teaspoon lemon juice and consume it several times a day.\n- Boil a cup of water and add one-half or one teaspoon of cinnamon powder. If you do not have cinnamon in powder form then simply use a cinnamon stick. Allow it to steep for a few minutes and then filter the water. If you need, you can add one tablespoon of honey. Sip it slowly.\n- Add one tablespoon of dried mint leaves to a cup of hot water. Allow it to steep for 5 to 10 minutes. Filter and drink this tea.\n- Add one tablespoon fennel seeds powder in a cup of boiling water and allow it to steep for 10 minutes. Filter and drink this 